hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18001","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Burdah, he said: I heard al-Agharr, a man from Juhaynah, narrating to Ibn Umar that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day."
"18002","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, he said: Abu Burdah narrated to us from al-Agharr al-Muzani, he said, and he had companionship: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed my heart is clouded, so I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times a day."
"18003","Affan narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Thabit informed us from Abu Burdah from al-Agharr, the Agharr of Muzaynah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed my heart is clouded until I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times."
"18004","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, he said: I heard Abu Burdah narrating that he heard a man from Juhaynah called al-Agharr narrating to Ibn Umar that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day."
